    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Bryce Harper** (75.57) leads the charge as our strongest play, buoyed by an elite 0.403 xwOBA and a favorable matchup against Abbott, who struggles with a 5.07 xERA. **Taylor Ward** (66.58) and **Geraldo Perdomo** (66.51) are also locked in as high-efficiency starters. **Taylor Ward** leverages a massive 16% park factor boost and a favorable platoon advantage against Boyd, while **Geraldo Perdomo** benefits from M\u00e1rquez\u2019s porous 5.64 xERA, providing a high floor for production. We are particularly attentive to our \"speed-first\" priority; both **Tyler Freeman** (61.39) and **Daulton Varsho** (55.18) gain utility from their respective matchups against slow-delivery pitchers, increasing their likelihood of swiping bags\u2014our most scarce category.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved **Jung Hoo Lee** (43.94), who barely missed the cut. While he maintains a solid projection against Miles, he ultimately fell behind **Luis Arraez** (46.48) and **Dylan Beavers** (44.00) due to lower efficiency relative to the park factors and SP skill metrics. **JJ Bleday** (39.25) was also considered but remained benched as he failed to clear our 40.0 efficiency threshold against a difficult arm in Wheeler. We are maintaining a cautious stance on **Dylan Beavers**, who, despite the park boost, faces a challenge with an elite hold against Boyd that suppresses his immediate upside. Keep an eye on **Cal Raleigh** (50.59); while his power profile is reliable, his score is slightly tempered by a difficult matchup against Meyer. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains unavailable due to his IL designation, so we will look to **Jonathan Aranda** and **Gavin Sheets** to shoulder the load in the heart of the lineup today.",
